    commentIndustry: "Structurally pressured: imports ~26% of local supply (+39.7% y/y), concentrated in Astral's own frozen bone-in / tertiary mix; anti-dumping duties ineffective at current levels; AGOA quota overhang. Astral is #1 domestic (~27%), but ~20% once imports are counted. Pricing power elusive (FY25 broiler margin just 1.5%); the H1 2026 recovery to 9.3% was driven 'primarily' by a maize price collapse, not structure. A Competition Commission poultry inquiry is underway. Base revenue CAGR ~3-5%, the high case contingent on the Poultry Master Plan curbing imports. NOTE: did not clear Rapid Triage (deprioritised).",
    commentMoat: "Domestic cost/scale leadership: rising Performance Efficiency Factor, exclusive SA Ross 308 genetics (Aviagen agreement), an explicit 'best-cost integrated producer' strategy. But the product mix is commodity-heavy (value-added only ~7%), and the moat does NOT protect against structurally lower-cost Brazilian imports that target the ~21-22% tertiary/offal slice of Astral's own sales. The margin recovery reads as lagging/cyclical (coincided with the maize collapse), not moat-widening.",
    commentManagement: "Through-cycle ROIC estimated ~21% vs ~13-15% WACC (model off the through-cycle figure, not the cyclically inflated H1). Conservative balance sheet: zero debt, net cash R1.15bn; ~2x-cover dividend flexed 220c->1,160c. Board separated, 75%+ independent NEDs. CEO an internal promotion (Arnold, ~28 yrs) lowering key-man risk, though both top seats turned over within ~18 months. ESG hurdles added to the LTIP (weighting unconfirmed).",
    commentSustainability: "B-BBEE improved to Level 5 (from 7/8) but behind sector comparator Tiger Brands (Level 1). Mixed environmental record (water recycling up; Scope 2 +10.5%; minimal renewables ~0.43%; Scope 3 excluded); DitchCarbon scored 14/100. Real quantified costs/risks: ~R10m/month emergency power & water; a March 2025 cyber incident (~R20m, ~2 days downtime, re-ranked to the #2 risk); HPAI vaccination only ~30% of breeding stock. ESG report not independently assured.",
    commentMacro: "Overlay: HEADWIND - draft. Modest net cost-side rand headwind (imported feed inputs, ~37% of feed cost, vs ~97.6% SA revenue). High commodity/weather sensitivity (maize/soya = 66-70% of live-bird cost; El Nino/drought risk to the 2026/27 season threatens the margin recovery); AGOA/US-tariff overhang; unresolved Competition Commission timeline. The only clear tailwind is near-zero rate sensitivity (debt-free).",
