    commentManagement: "THE CORE WEAK PILLAR: group ROIC < WACC for ~6 years (ROCE ex-goodwill 10.9% FY26 vs ~11.5-12.5% WACC) - value destroyed at the group level. M&A bifurcated: excellent domestically (Jet ~70% IRR, R1.6bn accretion) but poor abroad (London/Australia impaired R1.0bn). Pay-for-performance demonstrated (FY26 exec bonuses cut to zero; CEO total R18.5m from R28.5m); cut-sequencing sound. Blemish: a R1.0bn buyback at ~R100-126 with the stock now ~R57. Founder-Chairman bought ~R81m at the lows.",
    commentSustainability: "Cleanest pillar: no stranded assets, immaterial Scope-1/carbon-tax exposure; solar + 75% renewable electricity at TFG London. B-BBEE Level 2 (improved from 3); governance King IV-compliant with an all-independent Audit Committee; disclosure advancing ahead of peers (TCFD -> IFRS S1/S2). Residual cautions: qualitative environmental targets, uncontrolled Scope-3 supply chain, external ESG assurance not confirmed, responsible-lending vs rising bad-debt tension.",
    commentMacro: "Overlay: NEUTRAL, tilting TAILWIND (12-18 months). Highly cyclical, ~68% SA/Africa; offshore 32% is GBP/AUD discretionary retail (no export/defensive ballast). Clearest tailwind = the SA rate-cutting cycle (lower finance costs on ~R8bn debt + mass-market credit relief + lower discount rate; SA 10yr ~8.8%). Net rand broadly neutral; offshore FAILED to diversify in FY26 (all three markets weak at once). Concentrates the SA-consumer/rate factor.",
